<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pasuruan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pasuruan is a port city on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a> Strait. In the sixteenth and early seventeenth centuries it was a Muslim coastal state allied with Surabaya, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-agung">Sultan Agung of Mataram</a> conquered it in 1617. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule it became a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pasuruan.jpg" alt="Pasuruan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vebra · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masjid_Jami%27_Al-Anwar_Pasuruan_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
